{"version":"1","id":"codemonkeyunity","handle":"codemonkeyunity","name":"Code Monkey","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--mgoqDIgw--/f_auto/v1727446687/logos/codemonkeyunity","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.9089,"y":-6.9567,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":354,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T14:00:38.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2025-02-26T18:00:07.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.063559,"listicle_ratio":0.090395,"question_ratio":0.042373,"avg_read_time":5.898305,"summary_length_avg":475.395425,"title_length_avg":56.974576,"title_length_var":162.96263,"tag_entropy":2.575714,"tag_diversity":0.177966,"top_tag_share":0.381356,"avg_upvotes":0.949153,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.121469,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.130564,"zero_engagement_share":0.725989,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":5.698682,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.566372},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-3.6618,8.8676],"cadence_depth":[7.2647,0.1029],"hype_variety":[8.7059,-5.8382],"title_style":[4.7794,9.3088]},"top_tags":[["game-development",248],["unity",163],["gaming",66],["c#",61],["steam",48],["game-design",24],["marketing",21],["physics",13]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Solo indie game developers earning millions on Steam","Why indie developers should not fear sharing their game ideas","To Learn Anything, First Learn Self-Discipline"],"outlier":["Unity AI lets you generate Sprites, Textures, Animations, Materials and Textures! #unity #sponsored"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"esovRRajM","title":"Should you build your own game engine or just make a game","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MCxG_Kq2jR4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/should-you-build-a-game-engine--esovrrajm","summary":"A short take on whether developers should build their own game engine or use an existing one. The core argument is that building a game engine and making a game are two separate goals that rarely coexist well. Custom engine development requires mastering rendering APIs (DirectX, Vulkan), physics engines, asset pipelines, and language choices before any actual game work begins. For those who want to make games, commercially available engines like Unreal, Unity, and Godot are recommended as the practical path.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MCxG_Kq2jR4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T14:00:38.000Z"},{"id":"grwVQvJFb","title":"10 playtesting lessons every indie game developer should know","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WB6Ui5XeH0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-10-secrets-to-making-better-games--grwvqvjfb","summary":"A breakdown of 10 common mistakes revealed through playtesting across 22 indie games, including: static main menus signaling an unfinished product, missing controller/keyboard tutorial parity, shipping broken demo content, omitting the game name from the main menu, ignoring known bugs, content balance issues, unfair punishing mechanics, keeping unfun mechanics out of attachment, missing tutorials, and relying on text-only tutorials. The post emphasizes that developers suffer from the 'curse of knowledge' and can never see their game with fresh eyes, making regular playtesting essential. A practical playtesting pipeline is outlined: start with friends and family, then Reddit/Discord communities, then Steam playtesting, then a public free demo, and finally Steam Next Fest.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_WB6Ui5XeH0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T15:00:58.000Z"},{"id":"eRBlERiEp","title":"Free 5-hour Unity 2D game development course for beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=spDmgXUgj6Y","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/free-course-on-making-an-awesome-unity-2d-game--erbleriep","summary":"A free 5-hour YouTube course covering Unity 2D game development from scratch. Topics include physics, input handling, collision detection, UI, and clean C# code practices. The course mirrors the instructor's own professional workflow for Steam game development, guiding learners step by step from an empty project to a polished final game.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/spDmgXUgj6Y/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T14:01:28.000Z"},{"id":"0WpQAhk2j","title":"Buy vs build in game dev depends on how much your time is worth","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i79-VvzwmVo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-much-is-your-time-worth--0wpqahk2j","summary":"A cost-benefit argument for buying game development assets versus building them from scratch. Using the Unity Asset Store summer sale as context, the author frames the buy-vs-build decision around the value of a developer's time. The example used is the author's own asset pack (36 tools for $36), arguing that unless your hourly rate is extremely low, purchasing pre-built tools is almost always more economical than building them yourself.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/i79-VvzwmVo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T14:01:24.000Z"},{"id":"KHBSSu8bB","title":"What I DON'T want to happen to YOU!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hg5u-qEIoDo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-i-don-t-want-to-happen-to-you--khbssu8bb","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Hg5u-qEIoDo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T15:00:35.000Z"},{"id":"QgcJktQbi","title":"Unity AI is SUPER USEFUL and now in Open Beta! #sponsored","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lcR8Fj-iUpw","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-ai-is-super-useful-and-now-in-open-beta-sponsored-qgcjktqbi","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lcR8Fj-iUpw/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T12:51:21.000Z"},{"id":"N9tK90xqL","title":"5 MORE Beginner Projects for you to BUILD!","url":"https://www.youtube.c